     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022;	The project has partnered with the Ministry of Environment and Climate Change (MoECC) and has completed contextual analysis and mapping of climate security institutions and actors. 
&#x2022;	A tailor-made training module was developed and 60 participants (M:36, F:24) representing officials from climate and security-relevant institutions were engaged in a training workshop on the climate-security nexus.
&#x2022;	Adopting an agreed set of criteria, UNDP supported identifying three hotspot communities for piloting climate security actions at the local level. 
&#x2022;	In partnership with the Berghoff Foundation and Save the Children, UNDP mobilized the local leaders and stakeholders in a consultative process to determine climate-related security risks and prioritized mitigation actions.
&#x2022;	UNDP in collaboration with the Sida, and in partnership with the Ministry of Environment and Climate Change, completed a deep dive review and consultations on environmental sustainability in a conflict-affected fragile country in Somalia. 
&#x2022;	Four (4) Stockholm+50 consultations involving 184 (M:119 F:65) have been organized in 2022 involving a varied groups and stakeholders at all levels together with the government, partners, UN agencies and the Embassy of Sweden.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
